WHPX's APIC EOI exit takes the BQL around ioapic_eoi_broadcast(). The
vCPU loop runs without the BQL, and a device raises or lowers its line
(ioapic_set_irq) under it from another vCPU. Unlocked, the EOI's clearing
of Remote IRR and its test of irr interleave with the raise's setting of
irr and its test of Remote IRR: neither delivers, and a level-triggered
line stays high with nothing ever serviced again (it never changes level
again). d3dpt-vga's INTx under a Windows 11 desktop composing at 60
frames/s lost its interrupt so within a minute: a TDR with every fence
done and the last one never reported (track M25). Drop when upstream
locks it (or takes the EOI exit outside the unlocked loop).

diff --git a/target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c b/target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c
index b3bd765..d22c6eb 100644
--- a/target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c
+++ b/target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c
@@ -2352,7 +2352,17 @@ int whpx_vcpu_run(CPUState *cpu)
 
         case WHvRunVpExitReasonX64ApicEoi:
             assert(whpx_irqchip_in_kernel());
+            /*
+             * The loop runs without the BQL, and a device raises its line
+             * (ioapic_set_irq) under it from another vCPU: unlocked, the
+             * EOI's clearing of Remote IRR and its look at irr interleave
+             * with the raise's setting of irr and its look at Remote IRR,
+             * neither delivers, and a level-triggered line stays high
+             * with nothing ever serviced again.
+             */
+            bql_lock();
             ioapic_eoi_broadcast(vcpu->exit_ctx.ApicEoi.InterruptVector);
+            bql_unlock();
             break;
 
         case WHvRunVpExitReasonX64Halt:
